      "options": {
        "content": "GPU metrics come from `exporters/gpu/gpu_exporter.py` running on WSL against `/usr/lib/wsl/lib/nvidia-smi`, so they describe the Windows GPU through WSL's passthrough. `windows_exporter`'s own `gpu` collector reports nothing on WSL2 hosts, which is why this exporter exists. Per-process memory is only emitted when nvidia-smi can read it; under WSL it reports `[N/A]` for Windows-side processes, so 'Memory held per process' is normally empty while 'Compute processes' still counts them.",
